        "min": 2,
        "texto": "Today you learn to greet people in Russian. First, listen: «Привет!» (pree-VYET) is for a friend, and «Здравствуйте!» (ZDRAH-stvooy-tyeh) is for a stranger or for your boss. Then come the last six letters of this lesson: «л», «п» and «ф» sound like in English. But «ц» (ts), «ч» (ch) and «ш» (sh) are sounds that need attention."
